.TH CLIP 1 clip-VERSION
.SH NAME
clip \- print the X11 CLIPBOARD selection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clip
[
.B \-h
|
.BR \-\-help
|
.B \-help
]
[
.B \-v
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clip
prints the contents of the X11
.BR CLIPBOARD
selection to standard output as UTF-8 text. It supports both normal and INCR
transfer protocols.
.PP
If there is no owner for the
.BR CLIPBOARD
selection, nothing is printed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help, \-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-v
Display version information and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, non-zero on error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Copy text into the clipboard (using xsel) and print it:
.B echo hello | xsel \/\-bi ; clip
